{"id": "EUVD-2026-102335", "enisaUuid": "be91c6a9-38a9-3619-88d3-8f9f6db3fb66", "description": "Netgate pfSense CE 2.7.0 through 2.9.0 contains a configuration injection vulnerability that allows authenticated users with IPsec Mobile privileges to execute commands as root via the login_banner field. Attackers can submit a single-line banner containing '}' to escape the unquoted strongswan.conf attr value and define charon.start-scripts entries that charon executes as root on restart.", "datePublished": "2026-10-15T18:46:23", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-15T20:04:59", "baseScore": 8.6, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:H/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/abraxas/pfsense-ipsec-login-banner", "https://abraxaslabs.tech/research/pfsense-ce-leftovers", "https://abraxaslabs.tech/research/pfsense-ipsec-login-banner", "https://github.com/pfsense/pfsense/blob/9363ac5b8651a1c7a333180425ce7719070f95f9/src/etc/inc/ipsec.inc#L1361-L1388", "https://github.com/pfsense/pfsense/blob/9363ac5b8651a1c7a333180425ce7719070f95f9/src/etc/inc/ipsec.inc#L1842-L1845", "https://github.com/pfsense/pfsense/blob/9363ac5b8651a1c7a333180425ce7719070f95f9/src/usr/local/www/vpn_ipsec_mobile.php#L269-L273", "https://github.com/pfsense/pfsense/commit/27a52d0807", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/netgate-pfsense-ce-2.7.0-through-2.9.0-command-injection-via-ipsec-mobile-login-banner"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-111223", "GHSA-743j-3p3m-6h73"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.71, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "9b90008a-c4fa-37ad-a610-7b14e4e9df36", "product": {"name": "pfSense CE", "vendor": {"name": "Netgate"}}, "product_version": "2.7.0 \u22642.9.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "695654b6-5909-3b68-b94e-e3e09fbca9a0", "vendor": {"name": "Netgate"}}], "isExploited": false}